# RopeTool.Mod's own insert clamps a too-large pos to the end
# (Ropes.Mod's Insert itself clamps, giving "hello world!"); Ropes.Insert
# instead raises Ada.Strings.Index_Error for BEFORE - 1 > Length
# (Source) (BEFORE = Length (Source) + 1, i.e. 12, is the one valid
# append position past the literal end; 100 is not) -- see PLAN.md's
# "Modification" section on why Ropes.Mod's clamping was not carried
# over wholesale.
program rope_tool
arg insert
arg hello world
arg 100
arg !
status 1
output
Error: BEFORE out of range
